course: dictionary
lesson: 3008
title: Dusty: dirt, dryness and dull colour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dusty is an adjective, so it describes a thing. In «the middle of the dusty road», dusty tells you what the road is like. Context clues help you find its meaning: a road with clouds of dirt rising from it is clearly not wet or clean.
explain: Look at the sentence: «Toad sat straight down in the middle of the dusty road.» A road that is dusty is dry, with lots of loose dirt that rises into the air when things pass. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: «the middle of the dry road with loose dirt» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Dusty can also describe a colour. Dusty pink is a soft, dull, greyish pink, not a bright one. The same word can describe a road, a room or a colour, so always look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Dusty means covered with dust, the dry powder of dirt that collects on things.
fact: A dusty road or place is dry, with lots of loose dirt in the air.
fact: Dusty can also mean a dull, greyish colour, as in dusty pink.
fact: Dusty is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «dusty old books» or «dusty shelves».
fact: Dust can make people with allergies or asthma sneeze or cough.
exercise: «Toad sat straight down in the middle of the dusty road.» What does dusty mean here? | *Dry, with loose dirt in the air | Very new and shiny | Quiet and empty of people | Wet and muddy
exercise: Which colour is dusty pink? | Pure white | *A dull, greyish pink | Bright, shiny red | Deep, dark blue
exercise: Tom says dusty means shiny and new. What does dusty really mean? | Bright and shiny | *Covered with dust | Wet from rain | Very loud
test: «He lies in the hedge by the dusty lane, thinking of the road.» What does dusty tell you about the lane? | Freshly painted | Covered in snow | *Dry, with loose dirt | Full of water
test: Why might a room in a story be described as dusty? | *Nobody has been there for a long time | It has just been cleaned | Everyone is dancing in it | It is full of sunshine
exam: Which sentence uses dusty to mean a dull, greyish colour? | The dusty lane was quiet all day | The dusty road led to the sea | *She painted the door dusty pink | Wipe the dusty shelves with a cloth
